  "reveal": {
    "brief_voiced": "Nan Pringle stands as the killer. The Colonel's tradition demands every place laid with a loaded pistol save those beside a lady, and thus Fifi Swain's neighbour at the third position upon the right should have faced an unloaded chamber. Yet the pistol at Nan Pringle's own place—the second position upon that same right side—remained charged. That weapon lay within her reach, and the length of the table's side offered her clear aim toward Fifi Swain.\n\nNan Pringle kept the Colonel's accounts and missed nothing; Fifi Swain, a lady's-maid, heard more than a servant ought. A poor relation, bound to ledgers and the household's secrets, would have cause to fear what a servant who listens might overhear, and what truths such overhearing might expose or unravel. A charged pistol at hand, and opportunity aligned.\n\nThe deviation betrayed the hand that held it.",
